    "description": "Summons a durable rope for {{math spellPower \"*\" 1}} hours, up to {{math spellPower \"*\" 3}} m long, obeys Caster's will, moves on command, and is easy to grab up to its full length. Resummoning replaces the old rope. In combat, can be sent toward a Target up to 15 m away. Triggers Will Test (Bonus {{math spellPower \"*\" 1}}) vs. Target's Strength/Dexterity Test. On success, Roots the Target for 1 round. If success is 50+, the Target is Paralyzed for 1 round and takes 2d6 damage. On failure, the rope is destroyed. Test repeats at the start of each round or until dismissed.",
